Aim

To configure monitoring alerts for CPU, storage, and bandwidth usage in Oracle Cloud.

Requirements
Oracle Cloud Account
Running Compute Instance
Internet Connection
Step 1: Login to Oracle Cloud

Open:

Oracle Cloud Console

Enter:

Username
Password

Click:

Sign In

Step 2: Open Navigation Menu

Click:

☰ Menu (Top Left)

Step 3: Open Monitoring Service

Go to:

Observability & Management
→ Monitoring
→ Alarm Definitions

(If not visible, use search bar and type “Alarm Definitions”)

Step 4: Create Alarm

Click:

Create Alarm

Step 5: Enter Alarm Details

Fill:

Field	Value
Alarm Name	CPUAlert
Compartment	Your Compartment
Metric Namespace	oci_computeagent
Metric Name	CpuUtilization
Step 6: Select Target Resource

Under:

Resource Group / Dimension

Select:

Your Compute Instance
Step 7: Configure Threshold

Set:

Option	Value
Operator	Greater Than
Threshold	80

Meaning:

Alert triggers when CPU usage exceeds 80%.
Step 8: Configure Trigger Rule

Select:

Option	Value
Trigger Delay	1 minute
Interval	1 minute
Step 9: Configure Notification

Scroll down.

Under:

Notifications

Click:

Create Topic

Enter:

Topic Name = AlertTopic

Click:

Create

Now:

Add Subscription

Select:

Email

Enter:

Your Email Address

Click:

Create Subscription

Step 10: Verify Email

Open your email inbox.

You will receive:

Oracle Notification Email

Click:

Confirm Subscription

Without confirmation alerts will not work.

Step 11: Save Alarm

Click:

Create Alarm

Alarm is now active.

Step 12: Test Alert

To increase CPU usage:

Open compute instance terminal
Run:
yes > /dev/null &

This increases CPU load.

Wait 1–2 minutes.

Step 13: Check Alert Notification

Open email.

You will receive:

CPU usage exceeded threshold

This means alarm works correctly.

Step 14: Stop CPU Load

Run:

pkill yes

CPU usage returns normal.

Implementation & Result

Successfully:

Configured monitoring alarm
Set CPU usage threshold
Configured email notifications
Verified alert generation

Cloud monitoring alerts were configured successfully.
